international mobility options, volunteering and other ways to
change your trajectory.
</p>

<div class="hero-grid">

<div class="hero-stat">

<strong>Keep Multiple Paths Open</strong>

<span>
Don't allow one rejection, job, school or location to determine your future.
</span>

</div>

<div class="hero-stat">

<strong id="totalCount">
0
</strong>

<span>
Opportunities in this hub
</span>

</div>

</div>

</div>

</section>


<main class="dashboard">

<div class="container">


<!-- =========================
OPPORTUNITIES
SECTION 01
========================= -->

<section class="panel">

<div class="opportunity-header">

<h2>
01 / Opportunity Library
</h2>

<div class="result-count" id="resultCount">
Showing opportunities
</div>

</div>

<div
class="opportunity-grid"
id="opportunityGrid">
</div>

</section>


<!-- =========================
DISCOVERY STRATEGY
SECTION 02
========================= -->

<section class="panel">

<h2>
02 / Opportunity Strategy
</h2>

<div class="discovery">

<div class="discovery-box">

<h3>
Stop Searching in Only One Direction
</h3>

<p>
A strong opportunity strategy uses several pipelines simultaneously.
If employment is difficult, look at fellowships. If funding is difficult,
look at accelerators. If credentials are weak, look at apprenticeships,
mentorships and projects. If geography is limiting you, investigate
international mobility pathways.
</p>

<div class="path-grid">

<div class="path">
<strong>Career</strong>
<span>Jobs → internships → apprenticeships</span>
</div>

<div class="path">
<strong>Education</strong>
<span>Scholarships → fellowships → exchanges</span>
</div>

<div class="path">
<strong>Business</strong>
<span>Accelerators → grants → investors</span>
</div>

<div class="path">
<strong>Global</strong>
<span>Residencies → visas → mobility programs</span>
</div>

</div>

</div>

<div class="discovery-box">

<h3>
The 5-Path Rule
</h3>

<p>
Never let one rejection end your search. Maintain five different
opportunity categories at different stages.
</p>

<div class="warning">

<h3>
Example Pipeline
</h3>

<p>
1 active application<br>
2 opportunities being prepared<br>
3 opportunities under research<br>
5 opportunities saved for future cycles
</p>

</div>

</div>

</div>

</section>


<!-- =========================
WATCHLIST
SECTION 03
========================= -->

<section class="panel">

<h2>
03 / Your Opportunity Watchlist
</h2>

<div
class="opportunity-grid"
id="savedGrid">

<div class="warning">

<h3>
Nothing saved yet
</h3>

<p>
Save opportunities that are not right for you today but may become
valuable later. Opportunity searching works better as a pipeline
than as a one-time event.
</p>

</div>

</div>

</section>


<!-- =========================
TRACKER
SECTION 04
========================= -->

<section class="panel">

<h2>
04 / Application Pipeline
</h2>

<div class="tracker-grid">

<div class="tracker-stat">
<strong id="researchCount">0</strong>
<span>Researching</span>
</div>

<div class="tracker-stat">
<strong id="preparingCount">0</strong>
<span>Preparing</span>
</div>

<div class="tracker-stat">
<strong id="appliedCount">0</strong>
<span>Applied</span>
</div>

<div class="tracker-stat">
<strong id="wonCount">0</strong>
<span>Won</span>
</div>

</div>


<div class="tracker-form">

<input
id="trackName"
placeholder="Opportunity name">

<select id="trackStatus">

<option>Researching</option>
<option>Preparing</option>
<option>Applied</option>
<option>Rejected</option>
<option>Won</option>

</select>

<input
id="trackDate"
type="date">

<button
class="primary"
onclick="addApplication()">

Add

</button>

</div>


<div
class="tracker-list"
id="trackerList">
</div>

</section>


<!-- =========================
OPPORTUNITY INTELLIGENCE
SECTION 05
========================= -->

<section class="panel">

<h2>
05 / Opportunity Intelligence
</h2>

<div class="discovery">

<div class="discovery-box">

<h3>
A Rejection Is Data
</h3>

<p>
If you repeatedly apply to one class of opportunity and receive no
traction, don't simply apply harder. Change the variable: eligibility,
experience, evidence, geography, program type, timing, or target.
</p>

</div>

<div class="discovery-box">

<h3>
Search Before You Need It
</h3>

<p>
The best time to discover an alternative pathway is before the
current pathway fails. Build your watchlist while things are going
well.
</p>

</div>

</div>

</section>


</div>

</main>


<footer>

Opportunity Atlas • Search Wider • Build Options • Keep Moving

</footer>


